<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kaiserbrief</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Imperial Letter</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kaiserbrief was a letter of November 1870, drafted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otto-von-bismarck">Otto von Bismarck</a> and signed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-ii-of-bavaria">Ludwig II of Bavaria</a>, inviting King William I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> to take the title of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-emperor">German Emperor</a> on behalf of the German princes. Ludwig signed after Bismarck agreed to secret payments to him from the Guelph Fund. It prepared the proclamation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> on 18 January 1871.</p></div>
